Load rendering throttle, done safely: coalesce in the observer + timer wakeup.

Re-implements the load-time paint-storm coalescing that builds 465-467
shipped and build 468 reverted, WITHOUT the freeze regression.

Root-cause of the freeze (device-confirmed on build 469): on this port the
RenderingUpdate "RunLoopObserver" is a GLib activity observer that fires
only at RunLoop::Activity::BeforeWaiting -- i.e. only when the run loop
actually iterates (RunLoopGLib.cpp). Deferring rendering work while leaving
the observer merely "scheduled" does NOT self-heal: scheduleRenderingUpdate()
early-returns on isScheduled() and never calls breakToAllowRenderingUpdate(),
so once the page goes quiet nothing wakes the loop to re-fire the observer,
and the deferred update never runs -> permanent freeze (rAF counter wedged
at 1; deterministic repro: swipe while reddit.com loads). Builds 465-467's
one-shot-timer-in-scheduleRenderingUpdate had the same class of bug plus it
broke the m_isWaitingForRenderer compositor handshake.

Correct design: throttle in the observer callback
(renderingUpdateRunLoopObserverFired, which only runs when
!m_isWaitingForRenderer), and when deferring, INVALIDATE the observer and arm
a one-shot Timer for the remaining interval. The timer is the wakeup the run
loop otherwise lacks: on fire it calls scheduleRenderingUpdate(), which
re-arms the observer (and honours m_isWaitingForRenderer), so it fires and
proceeds once the interval has elapsed. Dirty regions accumulate between
updates, so each batched update paints the union once instead of once per
landing resource (~340 Mpx -> ~35-50% fewer painted px/load, device-measured
under the old throttle). The env patch's ProgressTracker main-load window
(Page::isRenderingThrottledForLoad) gates it; a 10s per-load safety cap
covers pages (reddit/onche) that hold the progress bar open indefinitely.

The m_isWaitingForRenderer / requestCompositionForRenderingUpdate handshake
is never touched: that path schedules the observer from its own completion
handler, independent of this timer.

Compositor gate (fixes the move-during-load freeze): shouldDeferRenderingUpdateForLoad()
returns false whenever isCompositionRequiredOrOngoing() is true. Moving during
a load scrolls on the compositor thread and reveals content whose tiles are
painted by updateRendering(); deferring that paint deadlocks the
composition<-tiles<-flush handshake -> m_isWaitingForRenderer sticks true and
the page never repaints again (device-repro'd on onche.org: rAF wedged at 1,
past the 10s cap, only Qt-chrome interaction unstuck it). So we only coalesce
during quiet load with no compositor activity -- which is exactly the
paint-storm case -- and never while scrolling/compositing.

Applies ON TOP of webkit-load-rendering-throttle-env.patch. Unset/0 = off (stock).

